{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/145221-glitch-question","id":145221,"title":"Glitch Question","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-21T20:48:13-07:00","id":145221,"title":"Glitch Question","content":"I am a bit confused on how glitches are acquired, specifically permanent glitches. According to page 184, you receive a permanent glitch by increasing your Primium. However, on page 108 it shows that you don't really acquire a glitch until rank 6. So which is correct? Gaining one everytime your Primium raises, or raising Primium to 6 and higher? Even above 6, your don't gain one every level as page 184 sort of suggests","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T04:44:30-07:00","id":145520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dessembrae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/145221-glitch-question#post145221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am a bit confused on how glitches are acquired, specifically permanent glitches. According to page 184, you receive a permanent glitch by increasing your Primium. However, on page 108 it shows that you don't really acquire a glitch until rank 6. So which is correct? Gaining one everytime your Primium raises, or raising Primium to 6 and higher? Even above 6, your don't gain one every level as page 184 sort of suggests</div> </div> </div> </div> The second one. <br /> <br /> You are misinterpreting the line on page 184. You gain a permanent glitch by increasing your Premium wasn't meant to imply &quot;every time you increase your Premium.&quot; It just means that raising your Premium causes Glitches eventually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-22T06:40:56-07:00","id":145627,"title":"","content":"Ok thanks for the clarification","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T20:02:19-07:00","id":152025,"title":"","content":"Me again with another glitch question.<br /> <br /> When it comes to gaining permanent glitches such as through compromise rolls or gaining Primium, are all of them able to be removed through a restoration facility? I say this because starting at Primium 6, you acquire a permanent glitch which would seem sort of strange if it could simply be removed later. By that logic, you could be Primium 10 and have no glitches if that is the case.<br /> <br /> Is this in fact the case? If so, Demons would be pretty unique amongst all the splats that they don't have any inherent weakness long term weakness from high power stats such as werewolf essence bleed or vampire blood requirements.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/444-dessembrae","name":"Dessembrae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar444_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T20:59:42-07:00","id":152072,"title":"","content":"The way I would (and have) ruled it is that while you can use a restoration facility to temporarily remove the glitch, unless you also bleed off your Primum (likely through the same process as removing the glitch as an extra option) you will develop a new glitch in time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3058-juvenaliansatyr","name":"JuvenalianSatyr","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3058_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T22:20:36-07:00","id":152144,"title":"","content":"You guys say that like breaking into a well fortified, and guarded facility; plugging yourself into it, gaining anywhere from 4- 12 successes in the allotted time (10 minutes per roll) and then escaping without being caught is easy. If a player manages to do that, don't you think they deserve not to have effects like bright pink hair, or freezing everything they touch bleeding into every cover?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T22:39:45-07:00","id":152155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/145221-glitch-question?p=152144#post152144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You guys say that like breaking into a well fortified, and guarded facility; plugging yourself into it, gaining anywhere from 4- 12 successes in the allotted time (10 minutes per roll) and then escaping without being caught is easy. If a player manages to do that, don't you think they deserve not to have effects like bright pink hair, or freezing everything they touch bleeding into every cover?</div> </div> </div> </div>Minor glitches run as benign as &quot;has a persistent natural hair or eye color&quot; and part of the fun of characters powerful enough to start picking up arcane quirks is seeing how those identifiers shape the way they go about their business, so being able to reroll for a chance to get a less severe glitch or shuffle a different existing one into the Primum-based slot is hardly a non-effect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-28T23:46:28-07:00","id":152192,"title":"","content":"I don't disagree with you. But with all the trouble it takes to get rid of a Glitch I personally believe that removing any of them from a facility is valid. If a character wants to keep their glitches and develop them with the character fine. But if another want's to be Glitch-Free as it were and there is a system in place to do just that why nullify the player that option?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1064-miss_minty","name":"miss_minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-29T00:25:08-07:00","id":152201,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>miss_minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/145221-glitch-question?p=152192#post152192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't disagree with you. But with all the trouble it takes to get rid of a Glitch I personally believe that removing any of them from a facility is valid. If a character wants to keep their glitches and develop them with the character fine. But if another want's to be Glitch-Free as it were and there is a system in place to do just that why nullify the player that option?</div> </div> </div> </div>If someone wants to be glitch free they can stay at Primum 5 <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> After all, completing the Cipher brings them up to 4... why would they buy up to such a point that they obtain a permanent glitch? <br /> <br /> And the option imo, is to speed up the losing of temporary glitches and permanent glitches gained from other sources <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}